    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've been seeing some intermittent issues where the thermal monitoring sensors report erratic spikes that don't seem to correlate perfectly with the deceleration curve. It's almost like the thermal management is acting up or being unpredictable right at the peak friction point. Do you think that could be a material instability issue, or is it more likely a sensor calibration error?",
